# fork/verify/known-failing — upstream tests that legitimately go red once the
# telemetry seam lands (series commits telemetry-analytics-off,
# telemetry-feedback-off, telemetry-statsig-strip, telemetry-defaults-none).
#
# Format: one nextest filterset expression per line ('#' comments, blank lines
# ignored).  Consumers OR the expressions together, e.g. to exclude them from
# the required-green set:
#   cargo nextest run -E "not ($(grep -v '^#' known-failing | grep . | paste -sd'|' - | sed 's/|/ or /g'))"
#
# Provenance: the telemetry-seam verification pass (fork/reference material:
# verify/telemetry-seam.md corrections), re-verified against the rust-v0.149.0
# tree.  The seam sets analytics_enabled to Some(false) for every layer, so
# every test that awaits a POST to /codex/analytics-events/events times out,
# and the otel default flip (types.rs:592 + otel.rs:21) plus the accepted
# Caveat A (user BYO OTLP metrics become inert) fail the two metrics tests.
#
# NOT in this list, deliberately (the verifier proved they keep passing):
# mcp-server lib.rs default-analytics assertions (assert an untouched constant
# or reset analytics_enabled themselves), app-server v2/analytics.rs :56/:81
# (mutate the config after load), and cli clap tests.
#
# The telemetry-seam series commit OWNS this file: it refines module-level
# entries to exact test names when it lands, and the diff-accounting check
# proves no upstream test outside this list was modified.

